1
00:00:13,714 --> 00:00:19,714
Trail Mix-Up is a comedy, animation film directed by Barry Cook.

2
00:00:27,428 --> 00:00:33,428
During a picnic, Baby Herman follows a beaver into a perilous
sawmill - with Roger Rabbit in frantic pursuit.

3
00:00:41,142 --> 00:00:47,142
Roger Rabbit (voice), played by Charles Fleischer.

4
00:00:54,857 --> 00:01:00,857
Jessica Rabbit (voice), played by Kathleen Turner.

5
00:01:08,571 --> 00:01:14,571
Young Baby Herman / Mrs. Herman (voice), played by April Winchell.

6
00:01:22,285 --> 00:01:28,285
Adult Baby Herman (voice), played by Lou Hirsch.

7
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Droopy Dog (voice), played by Corey Burton.

8
00:01:49,714 --> 00:01:55,714
Bear / Beaver (voice), played by Frank Welker.

9
00:02:03,428 --> 00:02:09,428
Tom Mix (1880–1940) was an American motion picture actor, director,
and writer whose career spanned from 1910 to 1935.

10
00:02:17,142 --> 00:02:23,142
During this time he appeared in 270 films and established
himself as the screen's most popular cowboy star.

11
00:02:30,857 --> 00:02:36,857
Mix's flair for showmanship set the standard for later
cowboy heroes such as Gene Autry and Roy Rogers.

12
00:02:44,571 --> 00:02:50,571
His horse Tony also became a celebrity who received his own fan mail.

13
00:02:58,285 --> 00:03:04,285
Born in Pennsylvania, Mix served in the United States Army
before moving to the Oklahoma Territory in 1902.

14
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Three years later, after working as a physical fitness instructor, bartender, and peace
officer, he was hired as a full-time cowboy for the Miller Brothers 101 Ranch.

15
00:03:25,714 --> 00:03:31,714
Soon after, Mix established himself as the star
attraction of the Millers' Wild West Show.

16
00:03:39,428 --> 00:03:45,428
In early 1910 Mix agreed to work as an actor and
wrangler for the Selig Polyscope Company.

17
00:03:53,142 --> 00:03:59,142
Mix alternated between working in films and in Wild West shows until
1913 when he went into the film business full-time.

18
00:04:06,857 --> 00:04:12,857
The following year he established his own production unit and
became a director and writer as well as an actor.

19
00:04:20,571 --> 00:04:26,571
His films for Selig were usually one and two-reel shorts that initially emphasized humor in the tradition of Will
Rogers but eventually moved into action-oriented stories that displayed Mix's riding and stunting prowess.

20
00:04:34,285 --> 00:04:40,285
In 1917 Mix left Selig and signed a contract with the Fox Film Corporation.

21
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
His earliest films for them were two-reel shorts but
within a year he switched to features.

22
00:05:01,714 --> 00:05:07,714
During his peak period in the 1920s Mix appeared in action-packed westerns filled
with fights and chases which often showed him doing his own stunt work.

23
00:05:15,428 --> 00:05:21,428
His films were also known for their location work in places such as
Arizona's Grand Canyon and Colorado's Royal Gorge.

24
00:05:29,142 --> 00:05:35,142
Among the notable directors that he worked with during this time were John Ford,
Sidney Franklin, Jack Conway, George Marshall, and Roy William Neill.

25
00:05:42,857 --> 00:05:48,857
His leading ladies included Louella Maxam, Colleen Moore, Esther
Ralston, Laura La Plante, Billie Dove and Clara Bow.

26
00:05:56,571 --> 00:06:02,571
In 1928, after eleven years and 86 films with Fox, Mix moved
to FBO Pictures for a series of five films.

27
00:06:10,285 --> 00:06:16,285
With the advent of sound, Mix abandoned his film career
and returned to working in Wild West shows.

28
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:30,000
He came back to films in 1932 for a series of nine sound features for Universal.

29
00:06:37,714 --> 00:06:43,714
In 1935, he appeared in his final film, a 15-chapter serial for Mascot Pictures.

30
00:06:51,428 --> 00:06:57,428
Mix died in an automobile accident in Arizona five years later.

31
00:07:05,142 --> 00:07:11,142
On February 8, 1960, Mix was awarded a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

32
00:07:18,857 --> 00:07:24,857
In 1998, Mix's film Sky High was added to the National
Film Registry by the Library of Congress.

33
00:07:32,571 --> 00:07:38,571
The film explores themes of camping, cartoon, bear, sawmill, geyser.

34
00:07:46,285 --> 00:07:52,285
The tone is lighthearted.
